---
import lightSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/run-costs-light.svg?raw';
import darkSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/run-costs-dark.svg?raw';
import Chart from './Chart.astro';
---

<Chart
  lightSvg={lightSvg}
  darkSvg={darkSvg}
  title="Where the $143 went"
  caption="Reported cost and wall clock per run over two days. It's the CLI's estimate on a subscription, not an invoice."
>
  Bar chart of reported model cost per run. Calibration on 91 earlier applicants: 14 minutes, 14 dollars 78. First night, 365 applications: 46 minutes, 53 dollars 74. Overnight arrivals, 153: 20 minutes, 23 dollars 58. Three runs after the review, all 812: 92 minutes, 48 of it rate-limited lookups, 45 dollars 29. Work-sample looks, 121: 5 dollars 34. About 143 dollars in all, calibration and re-runs included, or about 17 cents an application all-in.
</Chart>
